# Line endings are never translated in this repository.
#
# ARGOS hashes file bytes and checks the hash: every `tests/fixtures/**.raw.json`
# and `docs/research/fixtures/**` payload carries a recorded `raw_sha256`, and
# `tests/test_fixtures.py` fails when a fixture stops matching it. Git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF on the way to
# the working tree, which changes those bytes and therefore that hash.
#
# This is not a cosmetic preference. Core invariant 7 says raw data is immutable
# and `.claude/rules/data-integrity.md` says raw source payloads are linked by
# hash; a checkout that silently rewrites them breaks both before a single test
# runs. Measured on a fresh clone with the Git-for-Windows default: all four
# recorded fixtures failed their own integrity check. `book_yes.raw.json`
# arrived as 7,532 bytes hashing 8f95c861... against the 7,174 bytes hashing
# 510f03e4... that its own sidecar records, and the four `.meta.json` sidecars
# were rewritten the same way.
#
# `* -text` rather than a fixture-only rule, deliberately: the guarantee has to
# hold for a payload recorded next month by someone who did not read this file.
# An opt-in list protects only the paths somebody remembered to list.
* -text
